# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# Why this file exists: before it, processor/ and the root docs were stored with
# CRLF while server/ was stored with LF. A Windows checkout then rewrote every
# line of every file, so merges between the two of us conflicted on whole files
# instead of on the lines we had each actually edited. That is how the merge in
# f109ec5 was able to delete the entire processor without it looking obviously
# wrong.
#
# "text=auto eol=lf" means: store every text file with LF in git, and check it
# out with LF on every machine, Windows included. Java, Maven, VS Code and Git
# Bash all handle LF without complaint, and this way no tool ever has an excuse
# to rewrite a file it did not touch.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never examined for line endings, never converted. text=auto
# usually detects these on its own, but being explicit means a corrupt image or
# a truncated jar can never be blamed on normalization.
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.jar  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mov  binary
*.avi  binary
*.mkv  binary
*.webm binary
